 @theDiReW0lf  Ouch. You bought a graphics card right when the prices skyrocketed, and as far as I remember, the 2080 Ti is only about 20% stronger than the 1080 Ti.  It's an obvious pattern that every second generation comes with a significant performance boost.

The problem with PC gaming isn't just the overpriced components, it's that the hardware gets outdated quickly, and I'm convinced that Nvidia is crippling its older gpus with software upgrades. It's nothing new, Apple already paid fines for those things. The third big problem is that games come out terribly optimized.  TLOU is by far the worst PC port I've ever seen, and I've been playing games since the 90s.

I switched to a console for the same reason, I'm currently using an Xbox Series S and I'm honestly very happy.  Unfortunately my PC is too old and dying and I need much more powerful hardware as I'm changing jobs (modeling in Creo - ex Pro/Engineer) and that's why I've started thinking about a 1080 Ti, although I'm also considering something like a 3070 or  Rx 6700xt.
